  "enhanced_information": "The most likely cause of the patient's skin findings is dermal deposition of hemosiderin due to venous insufficiency, possibly exacerbated by the application of scented lotion and the use of enalapril. The presence of enlarged superficial veins, edema, and red-brown discoloration with indistinct margins over the medial ankles supports this conclusion.",
